cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Kerr–Penrose Black Hole Reactor"
abstract: >-
  An interactive browser simulation of a reactor that extracts rotational
  energy from a Kerr black hole through the Penrose process. Feed particles and
  split photons follow Kerr geodesics in the equatorial plane (RK4 in the affine
  parameter), each split conserves four-momentum exactly, the emission axis is
  optimized over directions whose fragment can escape, and the black hole's mass
  and spin evolve under the Hawking area theorem, with Hawking evaporation and
  optional prograde ISCO accretion. English and Turkish interfaces.
authors:
